From 3ca6cefc20995a54be0cc4109bd5351c9c7b6115 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuya Fujiwara <hzw1258@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 14:55:51 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 09/17] Add Shift+Space gesture for half-width space input

In Empty state, Shift+Space commits a literal half-width ASCII space
regardless of input mode, overriding the default bare-Space full-width
behavior. In Composing state, the gesture commits the current preedit
(like Enter) then appends a half-width space instead of triggering
conversion, ensuring users always end up with a literal space.

The feature is gated behind a new optional config setting
keys.shift_space_halfwidth (default false), preserving backward
compatibility. Wires KeysSettings through EngineConfig, adds the [keys]
section to default.toml, documents the key binding in README, and
includes tests for both enabled and default-off behavior.
